-/* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- * 77c-T3: Search lightbox — uniform background blur (remove rejected per-card look)
- *
- * NOT dim-scoped — this is a theme-independent rendering fix (the lightbox exists
- * in both themes). Placed here (last-loaded) rather than theme.css to avoid the
- * Tailwind recompile footgun (theme.css is raw-linked AND @import-ed into tailwind.css).
- *
- * Bug: on /search, opening the lightbox blurred each grid cover individually with
- * sharp footers, instead of the uniform background blur seen on /showcase.
- * Root cause: feature/76 gives #main-content `view-transition-name: main-content`
- * (theme.css:2433) for the cross-page crossfade. A non-`none` view-transition-name
- * makes the element a backdrop root even at rest, so the position:fixed lightbox
- * scrim's `backdrop-filter` (showcase.css:565) cannot sample the grid behind it →
- * each cover paints sharp; 77b footers (no backdrop-filter) stay sharp too.
- * Showcase strips the name unconditionally (theme.css:2442) AND hard-cuts its
- * transition, so it never crossfades; search DOES crossfade, so we must NOT strip
- * the name unconditionally (that would downgrade search's nav crossfade from the
- * custom Fluent fade at theme.css:2434-2435 to the default root fade).
- *
- * Fix: release the backdrop root while the lightbox is open, gated purely on the
- * Alpine open-state class (`:class="{ 'show': lightboxOpen }"`, search.html:23) via
- * `:has()` — zero JS. Specificity (1,3,0) beats base #main-content (1,0,0); last-loaded too.
- *
- * Scope of the nav-crossfade guarantee (honest): for normal in-page use the lightbox
- * is closed before any deliberate page change (the fixed scrim covers the sidebar, so
- * sidebar navigation isn't reachable while it's open) → #main-content keeps its name
- * during navigation and feature/76's custom Fluent crossfade (theme.css:2434-2435) is
- * preserved. The ONE edge that loses it: navigating away (browser back / programmatic
- * location change) WHILE the lightbox is still open — then the pageswap snapshot sees
- * `.show`, so the outgoing #main-content falls to the root snapshot for that single
